# Testing

- Enforce **100% line and branch** coverage via JaCoCo on production code.
- Allowed excludes only: `*Application`, `*Config`/`*Configuration`, `*Priming`, `package-info`. Do not widen excludes without review.
- Prefer smallest tests that still hit branches (Ponytail + coverage).
- Map story Given/When/Then (or AC-00N) to test methods when implementing stories.
- Unit tests live in `src/test`; prefer domain/application units for branches.
- Integration tests live in `apps/*/src/integrationTest` (`*IT.java`). Use `testing` module fixtures (`com.nammamedmate.testing.Containers`) + Testcontainers for HTTP + Postgres + Redis wiring. Add/update an IT when an endpoint needs DB/Redis/security end-to-end.
- ArchUnit rules in `apps/api` must stay green.

Commands:

```bash
make test              # unit tests
make integration-test  # Testcontainers ITs
make coverage          # unit + IT + jacocoTestCoverageVerification
make check             # full quality gates (includes ITs)
```
